# Line endings are normalised to LF in the index *and* in the working tree on
# every platform. `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is required: this repo is
# developed on a Windows host where `core.autocrlf=true` would otherwise write
# CRLF working-tree files, which fails `prettier --check` (.prettierrc.json
# sets "endOfLine": "lf") and reddens the CI lint gate. See T-001 finding A-001.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending-normalised. The CC-BY texture maps
# (THIRD_PARTY_ASSETS) and any future reference-data kernels land here.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.pdf  binary
*.bsp  binary
